Memark Knowledge Section Instructions
App Overview
Memark is a SAAS personal knowledge vault app that lets users capture links, notes, screenshots, PDFs, and voice memos via SMS text or share-sheet from other apps. Powered by AI, it auto-categorizes, summarizes, tags, scores relevance, and schedules spaced repetition reminders/digests to ensure users actually revisit their saves (fixing the "90% never go back" problem). Core flow: Inbound via Twilio (shared number for trial/all users — strict sender phone = user ID to prevent leaks; upgrade to dedicated unique number for premium privacy/throughput). Outbound sharing: Export to X threads, Notion pages, or social with referrals for virality. Platforms: iOS/Android (Expo/React Native) + web app (Next.js). Monetization: Subscriptions via Stripe ($9.99/mo shared/basic: 1k items/basic AI/search; $19.99/mo dedicated/unlimited: unique number, unlimited items, advanced AI agents/reminders/exports; $29.99/mo enterprise: teams/custom). Security: Supabase RLS, Twilio Verify for phone spoofing prevention on signup, row-level isolation (user sees only own data).
Key Features (Build Sequentially for Cohesiveness)

Capture/Inbound: SMS to Twilio number (shared for basic, dedicated for pro) — webhook parses sender phone as strict ID, creates item, triggers AI pipeline. Share-sheet integration (Expo: "Share to Memark" from browser/apps → save with previews/AI).
AI Magic: Auto-categorize/tag/summarize/score (OpenAI/Grok API). Spaced repetition feed/reminders (daily digests: "Revisit these?"). Semantic search with pgvector.
UI/UX: Clean Notion-like minimalism (purple #8B5CF6 primary, #EC4899 accents, white space, Inter/SF Pro fonts). ItemCard: Expandable with clickable URL, previews (title/desc/image/badge), haptics on tap/open. Collections: Purple line SVGs (replace multi-color — e.g., fork for recipes). Navigation: Bottom tabs (Feed, Collections, Search, Profile, Settings) — consistent icons/transitions.
In-App Browser: Mobile: Expo WebView like X (stay in app, reader mode toggle, share from browser, haptics). Web: Iframe/overlay popup (same page, close button).
Sharing/Network Effect: Inbound share-sheet saves privately with previews. Outbound: Export item/collection to X thread/Notion with referral ("via Memark [ref link]").
Linktree Profiles: Opt-in pro feature — ProfileScreen (/profile/[username]): Linktree-style list of public marks with previews. Toggle per item in ItemDetail (upgrade modal if not pro).
Settings/Admin: "Refresh All Previews" button (batch re-fetch for existing links). Upgrade banners/modals. Future admin dashboard for power users.
Subscriptions/Money: Stripe integration — plan checks (basic vs pro vs enterprise), trial flow (shared number), annual discounts (20% off).

Basic Needs for Award-Winning App (Industry Standards)

Cohesiveness: Unified design system (theme.ts with colors/fonts/spacing). Consistent branding (purple palette, logo/icon across all screens/platforms). All features tie back to core "anti-forget" vault (e.g., AI reminders in feed, previews in cards/profiles).
Consistency: UI patterns (e.g., expandable cards everywhere, haptics on all interactions, dark/light modes). Code style: TypeScript, ESLint, component reuse (e.g., PreviewCard for feed/profiles).
Easy Navigation: Intuitive bottom tabs, swipe gestures (Reanimated for smooth), global search bar. Accessibility: WCAG 2.1 (contrast ratios, screen reader support, keyboard nav).
Industry Standards:
Performance: Fast load (skeletons on fetch, lazy images, Supabase caching). Offline support (AsyncStorage for recent saves).
Security: Strict phone-ID (webhook/sender check), RLS, encryption for sensitive data, GDPR compliance.
Scalability: Supabase Pro ($25/mo at 50k MAU), Twilio throughput upgrades.
Monetization: Stripe Checkout/webhooks, trial (14 days shared), analytics (Mixpanel for churn/usage).
Testing: E2E (Detox/Cypress), unit (Jest), security audits (RLS tests).
Polish: Haptics/animations (Reanimated/Framer), responsive web (Next.js), PWA support.


Build iteratively: Start with core capture/AI/feed → add previews/browser → sharing/profiles → subscriptions/security. Ensure every change renders visually in preview (clear cache after). Use Cursor for fixes if Bolt lags. Aim for premium feel: Cohesive, consistent, easy — Memark owns the self-save space! 🚀  

## Scaling, Architecture, Design & UX Guidelines (Lean for 1M Users as Solo Founder)

**Scaling Principles**  
Auto-scale to 1M users with minimal ops and cost. Start free-tier MVP, grow with revenue.
- **User Capacity**: Supabase Pro ($25/mo base, 100k MAU included, ~$0.003/extra MAU). Twilio shared number trial (3 MPS, $2/mo + $0.01/msg); dedicated long-code for pro users ($1–2/extra/mo, charge premium).
- **Cost at 1M**: ~$5k/mo total (Supabase + Twilio + AI credits ~$0.01/query capped per user). Monitor via Supabase/Stripe dashboards (alerts for DB/storage/egress spikes).
- **Performance**: Lazy-load previews/images (Supabase CDN), cache AI results (edge functions TTL), offline recent items (AsyncStorage).
- **Ops**: No servers — serverless only. Automate alerts (Twilio SMS/email). Mixpanel (free to 100k events/mo) for usage/churn.
- **Future-Proof**: RLS strict everywhere, batch jobs (refresh previews, reminders), ready for AWS Lambda if needed (but keep Supabase core).

**Architecture (Serverless, Cross-Platform, Lean)**  
Minimal stack for one-person maintenance: Expo/React Native (mobile + web share 80%), Supabase (DB/auth/storage/realtime/edge), Twilio (SMS).
- **Frontend**: Expo/React Native (iOS/Android, haptics/share-sheet), Next.js web (SSR + PWA).
- **Backend**: Supabase Postgres (RLS: auth.uid() = user_id), edge functions (categorize-item, batch_refresh_previews, Twilio webhook).
- **Flow**: Inbound SMS/share → webhook (strict phone-ID) → save → AI + preview fetch → realtime feed update.
- **Data**: Users (phone primary, plan_type), Items (user_id, preview fields), Profiles (public_marks array, opt-in).
- **Security**: Twilio Verify signup, RLS, encrypt notes, GDPR export/delete in Settings.
- **Deployment**: Expo EAS mobile, Vercel web, GitHub Actions CI/CD.

**Design & UX (Award-Winning, Cohesive, Consistent, Accessible)**  
Notion-inspired minimalism: #8B5CF6 primary purple, #EC4899 accents, white space, Inter/SF Pro fonts, subtle shadows/gradients. Consistent across platforms.
- **Cohesiveness**: theme.ts (colors/fonts/spacing/haptics). All screens reinforce "vault" (secure, organized, revisit-focused).
- **Consistency**: Expandable ItemCard (previews/links), haptics on every interaction, dark/light auto-switch, custom purple line SVGs (no multi-color icons).
- **Easy Navigation**: Bottom tabs (Feed, Collections, Search, Profile, Settings), swipe gestures (Reanimated), global search bar, back/keyboard nav.
- **Industry Standards**:
  - Performance: Skeletons + lazy images, offline recent items.
  - Accessibility: WCAG 2.1 (4.5:1 contrast, screen reader, voiceover haptics).
  - Polish: Reanimated/Framer animations, responsive web, PWA support.
  - Testing: Unit (Jest), E2E (Detox/Cypress), RLS security tests.

**Build Order**  
1. Core capture (Twilio + share-sheet) → AI + feed/ItemCard.
2. Previews (OG/oEmbed) + browser (WebView/iframe).
3. Sharing (inbound/outbound with referrals) + profiles (Linktree opt-in).
4. Subscriptions (Stripe) + security (Verify/RLS).
5. Polish (haptics, icons, refresh button).

Clear cache (expo start --clear) after every change for visuals. This sets Memark for 1M users as a lean solo SAAS — premium, scalable, and viral! 🚀